# The verification programs that cannot pass on Linux (OpenSpec change m7-linux, design D6): <name><TAB><reason>, as
# known.list. A reason that starts with "windows" skips the program there; any other makes its failure known. Read
# by tools/legacy_tests/run_legacy_tests.py --platform linux. Each line was measured with QB64pe's Linux build too.
v16_m6_if_around_meta	line: $IF WIN is false on Linux, so the IF of line 4 has no END IF and we name line 4; lines are checked against Windows's recording, where QB64pe names line 7 (QB64pe's Linux build names line 4 of the auto-included vwatch_stub.bm)
v16_m6_split_block	line: $IF WIN is false on Linux, so the block crosses the $END IF and we name line 8; lines.list gives Windows's line 6 (QB64pe's Linux build names line 10)
v22_d_shell	windows: SHELLs cmd; on Linux the shell's "not found" comes between the program's lines in another order each run
v24_x93_large_bytes	varies: an array of 8 TB is allocated or "Out of memory" as the kernel's overcommit allows (allocated when recorded on 2026-10-28; "Out of memory" in WSL on 2026-11-02, QB64pe's Linux build too)
v24_x96_large_redim	varies: an array of 8 TB is allocated or "Out of memory" as the kernel's overcommit allows (allocated when recorded on 2026-10-28; "Out of memory" in WSL on 2026-11-02, QB64pe's Linux build too)
v29_a_sound_queue	varies: ALSA's null device plays nothing, so the queue's length changes from run to run; crashes now and then (munmap_chunk)
v29_d_volume_zero	varies: ALSA's null device plays nothing, so the queue's length changes from run to run
v29_f_queue_slice	varies: ALSA's null device plays nothing, so the queue's length changes from run to run; QB64pe's build crashed recording it
v29_g_voice	varies: ALSA's null device plays nothing, so the voices' lengths change from run to run
v39_c_files_raw_midi	varies: a raw sound on ALSA's null device crashes now and then, in QB64pe's build too (as corpus slice/s129)
v40_a_all_keys	windows: reads the executable's version information with PowerShell
v40_b_numeric_only	windows: reads the executable's version information with PowerShell
v40_c_order	windows: reads the executable's version information with PowerShell
v40_d_forms	windows: reads the executable's version information with PowerShell
v40_e_repeat	windows: reads the executable's version information with PowerShell
v40_f_with_icon	windows: reads the executable's version information with PowerShell
v40_g1_specials	windows: reads the executable's version information with PowerShell
v40_g5_gt_in_name	windows: reads the executable's version information with PowerShell
v40_g7_utf8_in_name	windows: reads the executable's version information with PowerShell
v40_g8_amp_in_comments	windows: reads the executable's version information with PowerShell
v40_h3_leading_zeros	windows: reads the executable's version information with PowerShell
v40_h6_largest	windows: reads the executable's version information with PowerShell
v40_i_places	windows: reads the executable's version information with PowerShell
v40_j_prefix	windows: reads the executable's version information with PowerShell
v40_k_only_product_version	windows: reads the executable's version information with PowerShell
v40_l_only_web	windows: reads the executable's version information with PowerShell
v45_sample	glibc: samples the C library's long double functions at run time; glibc's results differ from MinGW's in the last bits, on 772 of its lines (2026-11-04)
v57_j06_block_crosses_endif_agree	line: $IF WIN is false on Linux, so the DO crosses the $END IF and we name line 8; lines.list gives Windows's line 6 (QB64pe's Linux build names line 10)
